The role ladder : 
Read → Triage → Write → Maintain → Admin. 
Read views and comments. 
Triage adds managing issues and PRs, still no code push. 
Write pushes code. 
Maintain manages the repo but can't do destructive things. 
Admin can change settings and delete the repo. 

Codespaces vs github.dev :
github.dev: press . on any repo, free, browser editor, no terminal, no compute, cannot run or debug code. 
Codespaces: a container on a VM, full terminal, run and debug, billed by compute and storage with a free monthly quota, configured by .devcontainer/devcontainer.json, and prebuilds prepare that setup in advance so startup is fast. 
The test is always "do they need to run code?" If yes, Codespaces.
